WEBVTT

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.040
(SIGHS)

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.800
Yes, I know what that feels like.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.080
I don't want to forget this.
Somewhere out there is my family.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.400
Please, Marlin,
I can't find them on my own.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.840
I'll forget.
Please help me find my family.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.560
Yeah, Dad, you can get us all the way
across the ocean. Right?

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.280
No. (SIGHS)

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.760
But I know a guy.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.280
-Whoo-hoo!
-(MARLIN SCREAMING)

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.960
Righteous, righteous, righteous!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.480
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.640
Totally sick. Totally sick.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.240
I know. Isn't it great?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.760
No! I'm gonna be totally sick.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.720
It's the California current, dude.
It's got some gnarly chop.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.320
-(GROANING)
-Surf's up, dude!

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.840
(MARLIN SCREAMS AND GAGS)

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.360
Hey, dude, if you're gonna hurl,
just do me a solid...

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.600
head to the back of the shell,
lean out, and go for distance.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.760
We call that "feeding the fishes."

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.080
Correctamundo, Squirt!

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.160
And now we're looking for my parents
at the Brooch of the Atlantic? Or the--

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.320
-The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
-Exactly!

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.840
How are you gonna find your parents?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.800
Do you remember what they look like?

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.760
I'm a bit new to the memory thing,
so I can't say for sure...

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.560
but something tells me they were
mostly blue, with s-- Maybe yellow.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:42.400
That sounds right.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.160
Also I'm pretty sure I'm gonna know
them when I see them. We're family.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.040
By the way crossing the ocean
is the kind of thing you should...

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.200
only do once. One time!

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.800
Morro Bay, California's
coming up, dudes.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.080
DORY: Whoo-hoo!
Let's find my family.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.400
CRUSH: Go! Go! Go, go, go.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.840
NEMO: Just go, Dad.
MARLIN: Don't push me, Nemo.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.920
(MARLIN SCREAMING)

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.320
-(MARLIN GROANS)
-(NEMO LAUGHING)

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.320
Whoo-hoo! (LAUGHS)

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.760
SQUIRT: So long, Little Blue!
Hope you find your parents.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.760
CRUSH: And good luck
"feeding the fishes."

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.920
(TURTLES LAUGHING)

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.760
Too late. Already fed.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.160
Oh.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.600
This feels familiar. Mom! Dad!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.520
MARLIN: No. Dory! Dory! Wait! Wait.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.120
DORY: Mom! Dad!

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.880
MARLIN: Stop yelling for a second.
Do you really think your parents...

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.400
are just gonna be floating around here
waiting for you?

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.840
Well, I don't know, but there's only
one way to find out. Mom! Dad!

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.640
-Yell louder, Dory.
-Mom! Dad!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.520
-Sh!
-(GASPS) What was that?

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.920
Wait. I've heard that before.
I remember someone saying, "Sh."

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.040
Yes, well done. That was me.
One minute ago.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:49.800
ALL: Sh!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.040
(GASPS)

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:54.840
Please. Have you seen
my mommy and daddy?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.280
Their names are Jenny and Charlie.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.000
ALL: Sh!

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.080
(GASPS) Jenny and Charlie.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.040
MARLIN: What? Jenny and what?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.040
Those are their names!
My parents are Jenny and Charlie!

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.720
-Dory, wait!
-Jenny!

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.160
MARLIN: Can't we just take
a moment to come up with a plan?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.600
-Jenny! Charlie!
-Sh!

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.000
-Are you crazy?
-Sorry, she's a little excited.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.880
-Jenny! Charlie!
-Dory, stop yelling for a second.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.680
It's not a good idea
to come into a new neighborhood...

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.200
and call this much attention to yourself.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.320
You don't understand. I remembered
my parent's names! Jenny! Charlie!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.160
These crabs are locals and I
get the feeling they're shushing...

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.000
us for a reason. You might wake up
something dangerous.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.240
Are you talking about like
something with one big eye...

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.280
tentacles, and a snappy thing?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.040
Well, that's very specific,
but something like that, yes.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.200
You just in general don't want to--

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.640
(CRABS GASP)

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.720
Oh my goodness. Okay.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.360
There's a mistake. We're backing away.
Let us live and we will--

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.040
We'll worship you. We'll build a--
Do you like a monument?

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.880
(ALL SCREAMING)

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.040
(SCREAMING)

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.480
MARLIN: Oh! Ooh! Whoa!
Swim for your life!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.400
(ALL SCREAMING)

